 ],
 "text": "In 1843, Ada Lovelace published notes on Babidge's proposed analytical engine. Her note G laid out steps for calculating Bernoulli numbers, often called the first published computer algorithm. The engine was never completed in her lifetime. She also imagined it handling symbols beyond numbers, even music. Her story isn't only about predicting computers, it's about seeing possibilities in a machine that didn't yet exist."
